{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1376232667"}, "name":{"label":"Ytimacra"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-03-15T14:03:37-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0.1"}, "id":{"label":"12424861923"}, "title":{"label":"it works, but.."}, "content":{"label":"“touch grass” does exactly what it says itll do. it will block your apps until you literally touch grass. so why did i give it low review?\nwell, its that you can only block 2 apps, not 3, not 5, only 2. its not that it’s incapable of blocking more apps, its that its locked behind a subscription service. the problem is, its 7 bucks a month just to be able to block all my apps. alternatively, theres a yearly subscription for a more reasonable, yet still pricey 50 bucks. i know, i know, the dev’s got bills to pay, but i feel like a subscription isnt a good way to go about it. i would much rather pay for a one time fee, because a subscription is jus a bit much for an app that jus makes you touch grass. \nanyway, thats just my opinion. some people may be completely fine paying a subscription, and thats okay. ill jus stick to my free plan till something happens\n\nedit: after using touch grass for a bit, i have found a few bugs\n- sometimes while choosing a category to block, the menu goes black and i have to back out and reopen\n- after touching grass to unblock apps, only apps that were hand selected get reblocked after the timer, selected categories are not (you have to manually reblock it)", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6739589530&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
