{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1150449226"}, "name":{"label":"justlovett0"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-03-15T08:52:11-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0.1"}, "id":{"label":"12423866923"}, "title":{"label":"Great concept, works well"}, "content":{"label":"Absolutely works for me. I get up, touch grass, and then get 15 or 45 minutes of my no-no algorithm apps. I love it. The barrier to entry is light enough to not be annoying, but strong enough that it does make me pick up my phone less. But please dev! Add a flashlight button in the camera. Multiple times I pick up my phone for the night and have to go outside to find grass that’s in some sort of lit area. And grass detection though the app isn’t great in very dark scenes.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6739589530&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1407053245"}, "name":{"label":"bigfathippo21"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-03-15T08:49:04-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0.1"}, "id":{"label":"12423855680"}, "title":{"label":"Amazing App!"}, "content":{"label":"In an era where screen addiction is becoming a growing concern, Touch Grass offers a practical and effective way to encourage healthier device usage. This app helps users reduce screen time by allowing them to block distracting apps while providing reminders to engage in real-world activities. Its simple yet flexible approach makes it an excellent tool for those looking to create a better balance between digital and offline life. The issue with the Touch Grass app’s blocking system is that it relies on the user’s self-discipline, making it easy to bypass. While the app allows users to block distracting applications, it also provides the option to manually enable and disable them at any time. This creates a loophole where, instead of being forced to take a break, users can simply unblock an app whenever they feel tempted, effectively defeating the purpose of the restriction. Since there’s no mandatory cooldown or stricter enforcement, the feature functions more as a suggestion rather than a firm limit, allowing users to override their own restrictions with minimal effort", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6739589530&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id509136898"}, "name":{"label":"Cedezles Dockerstitz"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-03-15T07:40:29-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0.1"}, "id":{"label":"12423605346"}, "title":{"label":"Really good, but one tiny bug"}, "content":{"label":"After 12:00 when it should reblock my apps, it blocks the apps, but still displays the button to block them. Again, this is a really small bug, and it’s not that big of a deal. Other than this, my experience has been great so far, so it gets five stars.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6739589530&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
