{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id17315779"}, "name":{"label":"The Cleric"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-03-14T21:00:32-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.0.1"}, "id":{"label":"12421856606"}, "title":{"label":"Neat idea, practical problems"}, "content":{"label":"This is an intriguing app, but it has some practical limitations.  If it’s night time, the camera can’t tell I’m on the lawn, because it doesn’t turn the camera flash.  That seems like an easy fix, either to turn on the flash, or just not ask to touch grass when it’s night time, based on the phone’s location and time.  The greater problem is what will happen in the winter—will I have to dig through the snow before I can use my phone?", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=6739589530&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
